<.page_shell flash={@flash}>
  <.legal_page eyebrow="Terms" title="Terms of service" updated="17 July 2026">
    <p class="text-ink-muted text-lead font-light">
      These terms govern your use of Nila, operated by Kaguya Media Private
      Limited ("Nila", "we", "us"). By creating an account or using the service
      you agree to them. If you are agreeing on behalf of a firm, you confirm you
      are authorised to bind it.
    </p>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">What Nila does</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        Nila does a junior accountant's preparation work: you send an unstructured
        mess of documents, and Nila extracts, classifies, and drafts structured GST
        workings — registers, reconciliations, and import sheets — and flags the
        lines that need judgment. Nila is a tool that produces drafts for you to
        review. It is not your accountant, auditor, or tax adviser, and using it
        does not create a professional-client relationship with us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">You review; you file</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        Nila drafts, a human approves. Nila does not file returns or submit
        anything to any authority on your behalf. You are responsible for
        reviewing every output before you rely on it, for the accuracy and
        legality of what you ultimately file, and for the professional judgment
        applied to the lines Nila flags. The signature stays yours.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul class="marker:text-ink-faint text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 font-light">
        <li>
          You have the right to upload the documents you send us and to have us
          process them, including any client authorisation required.
        </li>
        <li>
          You keep your login credentials secure and are responsible for activity
          under your account.
        </li>
        <li>
          You will not use Nila unlawfully, to process data you have no right to,
          or in a way that disrupts the service.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Intellectual property</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        We and our licensors retain all rights in Nila, including its software,
        design, documentation, and branding. You retain ownership of the data and
        documents you provide. You grant us only the limited rights needed to
        host, process, transmit, and display that material to operate the service
        for you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">No warranty</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        The service is provided "as is" and "as available". Automated extraction
        and classification can be wrong, and Nila's flags are aids, not
        guarantees. To the fullest extent permitted by law we disclaim all
        warranties, express or implied, including fitness for a particular
        purpose and that the output is accurate, complete, or compliant. The
        output is a draft for your review — not tax, legal, or accounting advice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Nila is not liable for any
        indirect, incidental, or consequential loss, or for any penalties,
        interest, or tax liability arising from returns you prepare or file using
        our output. Our total liability for any claim relating to the service is
        limited to the fees you paid us for it in the three months before the
        claim arose. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited under
        law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Fees</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        Where the service is paid, fees, billing cycle, and taxes are as set out in
        your order or plan. Fees are exclusive of applicable GST unless stated
        otherwise.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Suspension &amp; termination</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        You may stop using Nila and close your account at any time. We may suspend
        or terminate access if these terms are breached or the service is misused.
        On termination, your data is handled as described in the <.text_link
          navigate={~p"/privacy"}
          class="font-medium"
        >
          privacy policy
        </.text_link>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Governing law</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at Chennai,
        Tamil Nadu have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="border-base-300/60 border-t pt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-h4 font-normal">Changes</h2>
      <p class="text-body text-ink-muted mt-3 font-light">
        We may update these terms as the service evolves. Material changes will be
        posted here with a new date; continued use after a change means you accept
        the updated terms. Questions go to <.text_link
          href="mailto:hello@nila.tax"
          class="font-medium"
        >
          hello@nila.tax
        </.text_link>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </.legal_page>
</.page_shell>
